WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.308
- We have time for just one more story.

00:00:02.308 --> 00:00:03.552
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:06.570
(rock music)

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.770
So, you've all probably heard

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.348
of Cabbage Patch dolls, right?

00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:10.181
- [Audience] Yeah!

00:00:10.181 --> 00:00:11.014
- You've heard of Cabbage Patch?

00:00:11.014 --> 00:00:12.510
We're around the same age, nice.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.490
People went absolutely nuts for them

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.271
when they came out in 1983,

00:00:16.271 --> 00:00:17.700
the year after I was born.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.960
It was almost cool.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.310
The demand was insane though.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.300
These were everywhere.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.010
There's a new documentary detailing it all

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.757
called "Billion Dollar Babies:

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.450
"The True Story of the
Cabbage Patch Kids."

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.907
It's in theaters November 24th

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:31.650
and we actually have the
director on the line right now.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.570
So everybody say hi to Andrew Jenks.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.290
Come on!
(audience clapping)

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.391
What's up, Andrew?

00:00:38.391 --> 00:00:39.974
So, why this story?

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.220
- You know, it's crazy 'cause
when you go on YouTube even

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.620
and just look up Cabbage Patch Kids,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.330
you just see these insane
riots in malls and stores

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.640
and people going absolutely insane.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.880
And so, I started to
wonder like, why was that?

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.620
What was going on?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.630
And one thing about
the Cabbage Patch Kids,

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.950
which people may remember, is
the element of imagination.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.680
They built a hospital for
the Cabbage Patch Kids

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.570
called Babyland General.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:13.440
People dressed up in the
hospital with thousands of dolls

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.980
as doctors and nurses,
and there was ambulances.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.940
And so, it was just this
element of really believing

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.310
that they're not even dolls, they're kids.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.550
And in fact, people were going so crazy

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.580
that the company that was
making Cabbage Patch Kids

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.890
had to stop running commercials

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.320
because the government sued them

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.500
saying that the commercials
were harassing children

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.000
since they were promoting a doll

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.310
that you could no longer get in stores.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:44.400
So, they actually had to
stop running the commercials.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.840
They announced that

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.750
and that made people
wanna get them even more.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.060
So it just added to the craze.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.980
- Oh my God, what is wrong with humanity?

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.390
Of course, we wanted it more

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.520
now that somebody said
there's none available.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.410
So, well, that's intriguing.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.660
I did not know any of that actually.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.660
Everybody, to see more about
the Cabbage Patch Kids craze,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.570
check out Andrew's film,
"Billion Dollar Babies."

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.670
It's in theater's November 24th.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.780
Thank you so much, Andrew.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.011
I'm liking your post now.

00:02:11.011 --> 00:02:14.011
(audience cheering)

00:02:16.018 --> 00:02:16.851
All right, y'all.

00:02:16.851 --> 00:02:18.702
Well, we've hit that point

00:02:18.702 --> 00:02:20.990
when we usually give our guest $1,000

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.250
courtesy of our season
long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:26.160
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.080
But today, that's gonna go

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.520
to one lucky person in this audience.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.495
So anybody want some money?

00:02:31.495 --> 00:02:33.519
(audience cheering)

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.695
Keep your eye on this monitor.

00:02:35.695 --> 00:02:37.775
Someone's face is gonna pop up.

00:02:37.775 --> 00:02:40.775
(audience cheering)

00:02:42.042 --> 00:02:47.042
Faces, faces.
(audience cheering)

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.941
First of all, your hair looks fantastic.

00:03:01.941 --> 00:03:02.774
- Thank you.

00:03:02.774 --> 00:03:03.607
- [Kelly] Like a walking party.

00:03:03.607 --> 00:03:04.440
What's your name?

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.273
- Lisa.

00:03:05.273 --> 00:03:08.185
- [Kelly] Lisa, how are
you gonna spend the grand?

00:03:08.185 --> 00:03:09.631
- I don't know.

00:03:09.631 --> 00:03:10.464
(audience laughs)

00:03:10.464 --> 00:03:12.630
- Well, Lisa, have a little fun with it.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.190
Yeah, have a little fun with it.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.030
- I have four kids.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.410
I'm sure I can figure it out.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.243
- Okay.

00:03:17.243 --> 00:03:18.076
I have kids too.

00:03:18.076 --> 00:03:19.140
Spend it a little on them.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.460
Spend a little on yourself.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.603
Do this for me.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:23.760
A mama of four.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.290
God bless, let's give you a round.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.566
(audience clapping)

00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:27.399
Well, thank you Lisa.

00:03:27.399 --> 00:03:29.183
